WEBVTT

00:00:15.071 --> 00:00:16.955
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:16.956 --> 00:00:18.894
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:18.895 --> 00:00:20.159
The family business.

00:00:21.281 --> 00:00:23.357
Before dad died, he told me something.

00:00:23.427 --> 00:00:25.358
Something about you.
What's did he tell you?

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:26.920
He said that I might
have to kill you, Sam.

00:00:26.994 --> 00:00:28.344
What the hell is that supposed to mean?

00:00:28.345 --> 00:00:29.112
I don't know.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.513
Did he know the demon's plans for me?

00:00:30.517 --> 00:00:32.320
Am I supposed to go
dark side or something?

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:33.919
Who are you? Please.

00:00:34.322 --> 00:00:35.881
You're in danger.

00:00:35.907 --> 00:00:37.418
What's your name? Ava Wilson.

00:00:37.459 --> 00:00:39.670
You must be one of us. One of who?

00:00:39.678 --> 00:00:41.490
One of the psychics like me.

00:00:41.586 --> 00:00:43.341
There are others like us out there,

00:00:43.348 --> 00:00:45.142
And we're all part of something.

00:00:45.187 --> 00:00:46.973
I'm not part of anything, okay?

00:00:46.977 --> 00:00:47.693
Do you see this?

00:00:47.708 --> 00:00:50.093
I am getting married in eight weeks.

00:00:50.128 --> 00:00:51.563
You can't run from this,

00:00:51.565 --> 00:00:53.123
And you can't protect me.

00:00:55.926 --> 00:00:57.000
I can try.

00:00:57.087 --> 00:00:59.071
Maybe I can help.
You've done all you can.

00:00:59.105 --> 00:01:01.800
Just go back to your
fianc. You'll be safe there.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.613
Promise me you'll call, then.

00:01:03.706 --> 00:01:04.961
I promise.

00:01:05.338 --> 00:01:06.773
Ava...

00:01:30.538 --> 00:01:32.092
Most of the stuff is up here.

00:01:32.135 --> 00:01:34.221
Still can't believe
you're closing this house.

00:01:34.285 --> 00:01:36.150
My parents got engaged here.

00:01:36.656 --> 00:01:38.150
My grandparents too.

00:01:38.257 --> 00:01:40.150
Yeah, a lot of people did.

00:01:41.055 --> 00:01:43.080
Boxes are at the end of
the hall. Need any help?

00:01:43.148 --> 00:01:44.470
No, ma'am. I got it.

00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:53.131
He's gonna take our toys?

00:01:53.588 --> 00:01:55.570
Only the ones you
don't play with anymore.

00:01:56.078 --> 00:01:58.113
It's not like you don't
have enough already.

00:01:59.015 --> 00:02:01.342
Son of a bitch. Son of a bitch.

00:02:01.407 --> 00:02:02.750
Watch your mouth.

00:02:02.807 --> 00:02:04.251
Maggie said it first.

00:02:04.336 --> 00:02:05.781
Watch your mouth too, Maggie.

00:02:43.985 --> 00:02:45.353
Good night, Tabitha.

00:03:17.178 --> 00:03:18.851
Oh my god! Yes, yes are you there?

00:03:18.857 --> 00:03:21.052
Please you have to send someone now.

00:03:22.096 --> 00:03:23.223
There's been an accident.

00:03:23.226 --> 00:03:26.263
A man fell down my stairs,
and I don't know if he's...

00:03:26.298 --> 00:03:28.832
His head is like
completely turned around.

00:03:30.006 --> 00:03:32.450
Tyler, don't look! Don't look!

00:03:32.926 --> 00:03:33.882
Oh yes, yes!

00:03:34.558 --> 00:03:36.122
As soon as possible.

00:03:39.915 --> 00:03:42.193
Just hurry, please hurry!

00:03:42.507 --> 00:03:45.152
I don't know, I didn't
see how it happened.

00:03:59.726 --> 00:04:00.932
Yeah.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.792
Okay. Thanks, Ellen.

00:04:05.808 --> 00:04:07.831
What did she have to
say? She got nothing.

00:04:08.296 --> 00:04:10.442
Me, I've been checking every
database I can think of,

00:04:10.508 --> 00:04:12.003
Federal, state, and local.

00:04:12.086 --> 00:04:14.321
No one's heard anything
about Ava. She's just...

00:04:14.366 --> 00:04:16.060
Into thin air, you know?

00:04:16.957 --> 00:04:18.101
What about you?

00:04:18.188 --> 00:04:20.851
No, same as before. Sorry, man.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:23.853
Ellen did have one thing.

00:04:24.628 --> 00:04:26.952
A hotel in Cornwall, Connecticut,

00:04:27.026 --> 00:04:29.123
Two freak accidents in
the past three weeks.

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:30.842
Yeah, what's that have to do with Ava?

00:04:31.247 --> 00:04:32.512
It's a job.

00:04:32.517 --> 00:04:34.420
I mean, a lady drowned in the bathtub,

00:04:34.457 --> 00:04:36.603
Then a few days ago, a
guy falls down the stairs,

00:04:36.648 --> 00:04:38.150
Head turns a complete 180,

00:04:38.156 --> 00:04:40.121
Which isn't exactly normal, you know?

00:04:40.595 --> 00:04:42.122
Look, I don't know,
Dean, it might be nothing,

00:04:42.126 --> 00:04:44.343
But I told Ellen we'd
think about checking it out.

00:04:44.405 --> 00:04:46.312
You did? Yeah.

00:04:48.726 --> 00:04:51.141
You seem surprised. Yeah,
it's just, you know...

00:04:51.568 --> 00:04:54.642
Not the patented Sam
Winchester way, is it?

00:04:55.197 --> 00:04:56.570
What way is that?

00:04:56.648 --> 00:04:59.523
Just figured after Ava,
there'd be, you know, more

00:04:59.607 --> 00:05:04.073
Angst and droopy music and
staring out the rainy windows.

00:05:06.098 --> 00:05:07.682
I'll shut up now.

00:05:07.928 --> 00:05:08.951
Look,

00:05:08.956 --> 00:05:11.273
I'm the one who told
her to go back home.

00:05:12.086 --> 00:05:14.021
Now her fianc's dead,

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:17.010
And some demon has taken
her off to god knows where,

00:05:17.025 --> 00:05:18.303
You know?

00:05:19.568 --> 00:05:21.292
We've been looking for a month now,

00:05:21.937 --> 00:05:23.401
And we got nothing.

00:05:24.825 --> 00:05:26.533
So I'm not giving up on her, but

00:05:26.538 --> 00:05:28.693
I'm not gonna let
other people die either.

00:05:29.937 --> 00:05:32.273
We got to save as many people as we can.

00:05:34.566 --> 00:05:37.631
Wow, that attitude is just
way too healthy for me.

00:05:38.075 --> 00:05:40.373
I'm officially
uncomfortable now. Thank you.

00:05:43.528 --> 00:05:45.461
All right, call Ellen.
Tell her we'll take it.

00:05:59.546 --> 00:06:01.590
Dude, this is sweet.

00:06:02.005 --> 00:06:04.163
I never get to work jobs like this.

00:06:04.555 --> 00:06:05.961
Like what?

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:08.851
Old-School haunted houses. You know,

00:06:09.238 --> 00:06:11.981
Fog, secret passage ways,

00:06:11.986 --> 00:06:14.053
Sissy  british accents.

00:06:14.726 --> 00:06:17.372
Might even run into Fred and
Daphne while we're inside.

00:06:19.586 --> 00:06:21.662
Daphne... Love her.

00:06:25.138 --> 00:06:26.533
Hey, wait a sec.

00:06:27.938 --> 00:06:30.363
I'm not so sure haunted's the problem.

00:06:30.457 --> 00:06:31.541
What do you mean?

00:06:32.465 --> 00:06:33.783
You see this pattern here?

00:06:34.665 --> 00:06:37.460
That's a quincunx. It's a five-Spot.

00:06:38.107 --> 00:06:39.911
Five-Spot. Yeah.

00:06:39.935 --> 00:06:41.411
That's for hoodoo spellwork, isn't it?

00:06:41.417 --> 00:06:43.081
Right. Hey, you fill
this thing with bloodweed,

00:06:43.207 --> 00:06:45.191
You got a powerful charm
to ward off enemies.

00:06:45.258 --> 00:06:46.891
Except I don't see any bloodweed.

00:06:47.018 --> 00:06:48.973
Don't you think this
place is a little too

00:06:49.538 --> 00:06:51.110
White-Meat for hoodoo?

00:06:52.967 --> 00:06:54.122
Maybe.

00:07:00.047 --> 00:07:01.193
May I help you?

00:07:01.276 --> 00:07:04.163
Hi. Yeah, I'd like a room
for a couple of nights.

00:07:05.438 --> 00:07:06.313
Hey!

00:07:07.055 --> 00:07:09.461
Sorry about that. No problem.

00:07:09.545 --> 00:07:13.092
Well, congratulations. You could
be some of our final guests.

00:07:13.156 --> 00:07:15.491
Well, sounds vaguely ominous.

00:07:15.527 --> 00:07:18.340
No, I'm sorry. I mean, we're
closing at the end of the month.

00:07:19.358 --> 00:07:21.851
Let me guess. You guys
are here antiquing?

00:07:23.555 --> 00:07:26.172
How'd you know? You just look the type.

00:07:26.258 --> 00:07:28.042
So, a king-Size bed?

00:07:28.368 --> 00:07:30.402
What? No. No, no.

00:07:31.538 --> 00:07:34.130
Two singles. We're just brothers.

00:07:34.566 --> 00:07:37.483
Oh. Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:07:40.065 --> 00:07:42.010
What did you mean that
we looked the type?

00:07:43.805 --> 00:07:44.783
You know,

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:47.700
Speaking of antiques, you have a really

00:07:47.706 --> 00:07:49.672
Interesting urn on the front porch.

00:07:49.737 --> 00:07:51.632
Where did you get that?
You know, I have no idea.

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:52.760
It's been there forever.

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:55.100
Here you go, Mr. Mahogoff.

00:07:56.385 --> 00:07:58.672
You'll be staying in room 237.

00:07:59.538 --> 00:08:01.861
Sherwin, could you show these
gentlemen to their rooms?

00:08:03.058 --> 00:08:04.163
Let me guess...

00:08:04.665 --> 00:08:06.030
Antiquers?

00:08:08.336 --> 00:08:10.020
I can give you a hand with that bag.

00:08:10.025 --> 00:08:11.570
I got it. Okay.

00:08:12.486 --> 00:08:14.080
So the hotel's closing up, huh?

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:16.739
Yep. Miss Susan tried
to make a go of it,

00:08:16.822 --> 00:08:18.871
But the guests just don't
come like they used to.

00:08:19.027 --> 00:08:21.398
Still, it's a damn shame. Oh yeah?

00:08:21.429 --> 00:08:25.183
It may not look it anymore,
but this place was a palace.

00:08:25.246 --> 00:08:28.302
Two different vice-Presidents
laid their heads on our pillows.

00:08:28.566 --> 00:08:31.972
My parents worked here. I
practically grew up here.

00:08:32.427 --> 00:08:33.730
I'm gonna miss it.

00:08:34.598 --> 00:08:35.822
Here's your room.

00:08:41.918 --> 00:08:42.853
Thanks.

00:08:50.578 --> 00:08:53.161
You're not gonna cheap
out on me, are you, boy?

00:09:02.345 --> 00:09:03.560
What the...

00:09:04.536 --> 00:09:05.581
What?

00:09:06.286 --> 00:09:07.503
That's normal.

00:09:08.578 --> 00:09:10.430
Why the hell would anyone stay here?

00:09:10.437 --> 00:09:12.361
I'm amazed they kept
in business this long.

00:09:13.827 --> 00:09:17.403
All right, victim number one,
Joan Edison, 43 years old,

00:09:17.435 --> 00:09:19.891
A realtor handling
the sale of the hotel.

00:09:19.935 --> 00:09:23.072
And victim number two
was Larry Williams,

00:09:23.076 --> 00:09:24.890
Moving some stuff out to goodwill.

00:09:24.956 --> 00:09:27.053
Well, there's a connexion. They're
both tied up in shutting the place down.

00:09:27.115 --> 00:09:29.060
Yeah, maybe someone here
doesn't want to leave,

00:09:29.065 --> 00:09:30.691
And they're using hoodoo to fight back.

00:09:30.786 --> 00:09:32.790
Who do you think our witch
doctor is. This Susan lady?

00:09:32.896 --> 00:09:34.103
Doesn't seem likely.

00:09:34.175 --> 00:09:35.783
I mean, she's the one selling.

00:09:35.856 --> 00:09:37.203
So, what then, Sherwin?

00:09:38.708 --> 00:09:40.062
I don't know.

00:09:41.008 --> 00:09:42.721
Of course, the most
troubling question is,

00:09:42.727 --> 00:09:44.450
Why do these people assume we're gay?

00:09:44.515 --> 00:09:45.852
You are kind of butch.

00:09:46.235 --> 00:09:48.170
Probably think you're over compensating.

00:09:49.705 --> 00:09:50.850
Right.

00:10:06.875 --> 00:10:07.762
Hey.

00:10:09.506 --> 00:10:11.892
Look at that. More hoodoo.

00:10:24.987 --> 00:10:26.580
Hi, there. Hi.

00:10:26.598 --> 00:10:27.943
Everything  okay with your room?

00:10:28.005 --> 00:10:29.292
Yeah, yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:10:29.367 --> 00:10:31.050
Yeah, everything's great. Good.

00:10:35.037 --> 00:10:37.913
Well, I was just in the
middle of packing. So...

00:10:37.987 --> 00:10:41.372
Hey, are those antique dolls?

00:10:41.945 --> 00:10:43.763
'Cause this one, this one here,

00:10:43.768 --> 00:10:45.913
He's got a major doll
collection back home.

00:10:45.917 --> 00:10:47.423
Don't you? Huh?

00:10:50.587 --> 00:10:52.931
Big time. Big time.

00:10:53.027 --> 00:10:55.773
You think he could come in, well,
we could come in and take a look?

00:10:56.225 --> 00:10:58.912
I don't know. Please?
I mean, he loves them.

00:10:59.007 --> 00:10:59.970
He's not gonna tell you this,

00:10:59.977 --> 00:11:02.130
But he's always dressing them
up in little tiny outfits.

00:11:02.145 --> 00:11:05.430
You'd make his day. She would. Huh? Huh?

00:11:06.946 --> 00:11:08.091
It's true.

00:11:09.617 --> 00:11:11.640
Okay. Come on in. All right.

00:11:11.915 --> 00:11:12.820
All right!

00:11:18.065 --> 00:11:19.523
Wow.

00:11:20.507 --> 00:11:22.442
This is a lot of dolls.

00:11:22.505 --> 00:11:26.180
They're nice, you know.
They're not supercreepy at all.

00:11:26.876 --> 00:11:29.493
I suppose they are a little creepy.

00:11:29.538 --> 00:11:31.181
But they've been in the family forever.

00:11:31.198 --> 00:11:33.552
A lot of sentimental
value. What is this?

00:11:34.048 --> 00:11:35.803
The hotel? Yeah, that's right.

00:11:35.828 --> 00:11:37.382
Exact replica, custom-Built.

00:11:45.546 --> 00:11:47.160
His head got twisted around.

00:11:49.295 --> 00:11:50.671
What happened to it?

00:11:50.736 --> 00:11:52.162
Tyler, probably.

00:11:52.237 --> 00:11:53.473
Mommy.

00:11:54.658 --> 00:11:56.383
Maggie's being mean.

00:11:56.476 --> 00:11:58.813
Tyler, tell her I said to be nice, okay?

00:11:58.885 --> 00:12:02.150
Hey, Tyler. I see you broke
your doll. You want me to fix it?

00:12:02.217 --> 00:12:05.491
I didn't break it. I found it like that.

00:12:05.976 --> 00:12:09.873
Well, maybe Maggie did it.
No, neither of us did it.

00:12:09.886 --> 00:12:11.753
Grandma would get mad if we broke him.

00:12:11.846 --> 00:12:13.970
Tyler, she wouldn't get mad. Grandma?

00:12:15.156 --> 00:12:17.560
Grandma Rose. These were all her toys.

00:12:18.075 --> 00:12:19.442
Oh, really?

00:12:19.805 --> 00:12:21.501
Where's grandma Rose now?

00:12:21.736 --> 00:12:23.171
Up in her room.

00:12:23.558 --> 00:12:26.591
You know, I'd really
love to talk to Rose

00:12:26.596 --> 00:12:28.401
About her incredible doll... No.

00:12:31.066 --> 00:12:32.250
I  mean,

00:12:32.655 --> 00:12:34.081
I'm  afraid that's impossible.

00:12:34.175 --> 00:12:37.771
My mother's been very sick, and
she's not taking any visitors.

00:12:43.096 --> 00:12:44.620
What do you think?

00:12:44.708 --> 00:12:46.130
Dolls, hoodoo,

00:12:46.135 --> 00:12:48.110
Mysterious shut-In grandma?

00:12:48.138 --> 00:12:51.553
Well, dolls are used in all
kind of voodoo and hoodoo,

00:12:51.587 --> 00:12:54.321
Like curses and binding spells.

00:12:54.355 --> 00:12:56.390
Yeah, maybe we found our witch doctor.

00:12:56.485 --> 00:12:58.743
I'll go see what I can dig upon granny.

00:12:58.747 --> 00:13:01.373
You get online, check old obits,
freak accidents. That sort of things.

00:13:01.407 --> 00:13:03.430
See if she's whacked
anybody before. Right.

00:13:03.515 --> 00:13:05.970
Don't go surfing porn. It's
not the kind of whacking I mean.

00:13:11.506 --> 00:13:13.123
I've been meaning to ask...

00:13:13.126 --> 00:13:15.103
What sort of renovations
are you planning?

00:13:15.178 --> 00:13:16.470
They never told you?

00:13:16.478 --> 00:13:17.972
Told me what?

00:13:18.065 --> 00:13:20.903
Miss Thompson, we plan
on demolishing the hotel.

00:13:21.898 --> 00:13:24.170
Oh. I see.

00:13:25.428 --> 00:13:26.732
Excuse me.

00:14:52.466 --> 00:14:53.540
What happened?

00:14:54.227 --> 00:14:58.012
The maid went into turn down
the sheets, and he was just

00:14:58.496 --> 00:15:00.712
Hanging there. That's awful.

00:15:00.718 --> 00:15:02.033
He was a guest?

00:15:02.076 --> 00:15:03.990
He worked for the company
that bought the place.

00:15:06.447 --> 00:15:08.932
I don't understand. What?

00:15:08.956 --> 00:15:11.422
Had a lot of bad luck around here.

00:15:12.455 --> 00:15:15.393
Look, if you'd like to check
out, I'll give you a full refund.

00:15:15.415 --> 00:15:17.963
No, thanks. I don't scare that easy.

00:15:26.497 --> 00:15:27.873
There's been another one.

00:15:27.876 --> 00:15:29.673
Some guy just hung himself in his room.

00:15:30.325 --> 00:15:32.501
Yeah. I saw.

00:15:32.566 --> 00:15:34.102
We got figure this out and fast.

00:15:34.456 --> 00:15:35.992
What did you find out about granny?

00:15:37.725 --> 00:15:39.150
You're bossy.

00:15:40.965 --> 00:15:41.873
What?

00:15:43.096 --> 00:15:44.720
You're bossy.

00:15:45.946 --> 00:15:47.142
You're short.

00:15:48.336 --> 00:15:50.292
Are you drunk? Yeah.

00:15:51.078 --> 00:15:52.160
So?

00:15:52.477 --> 00:15:53.681
Stupid.

00:15:55.516 --> 00:15:57.473
Dude, what are you thinking?
We're working a case.

00:16:01.067 --> 00:16:04.042
That guy who hung himself...

00:16:06.377 --> 00:16:08.263
I couldn't save him. What
are you talking about?

00:16:08.336 --> 00:16:09.533
You didn't know. You
couldn't have done anything.

00:16:09.536 --> 00:16:11.160
That's an excuse, Dean.

00:16:12.617 --> 00:16:14.911
I should have found a way to save him.

00:16:16.467 --> 00:16:18.452
I should have saved Ava too.

00:16:18.927 --> 00:16:21.302
Well, you can't save
everyone. Even you said that.

00:16:21.396 --> 00:16:23.420
No, Dean, you don't
understand, all right?

00:16:23.435 --> 00:16:26.090
The more people I save,
the more I can change.

00:16:26.166 --> 00:16:28.702
Change what? My destiny, Dean.

00:16:31.266 --> 00:16:33.480
All right, time for
bed. Come on, sasquatch.

00:16:33.485 --> 00:16:34.501
Come on.

00:16:34.586 --> 00:16:37.140
I need you to watch out
for me. Yeah, I always do.

00:16:37.236 --> 00:16:40.260
No. No, no, no. You have
to watch out for me...

00:16:41.027 --> 00:16:42.401
All right?

00:16:42.935 --> 00:16:46.132
And if I ever turn into
something that I'm not...

00:16:48.995 --> 00:16:50.931
You have to kill me. Sam...

00:16:50.965 --> 00:16:53.391
Dean, dad told you
to do it. You have to.

00:16:54.155 --> 00:16:55.982
Yeah, well, dad's an ass.

00:16:56.358 --> 00:16:58.352
He never should have said
anything. I mean, you don't do that.

00:16:58.367 --> 00:17:00.190
You don't lay that
kinda crap on your kids.

00:17:00.255 --> 00:17:02.331
No, he was right to say it.

00:17:02.838 --> 00:17:05.012
Who knows what I might become?

00:17:05.095 --> 00:17:07.593
Even now, everyone around me dies.

00:17:07.685 --> 00:17:10.070
Well, I'm not dying, okay?

00:17:10.158 --> 00:17:11.753
And neither are you. Come on, sit down.

00:17:12.027 --> 00:17:15.551
No, please, Dean, you're
the only one who can do it.

00:17:15.946 --> 00:17:17.643
Promise me. Don't ask that of me.

00:17:17.718 --> 00:17:18.973
Dean, please.

00:17:18.977 --> 00:17:20.860
You have to promise me.

00:17:26.766 --> 00:17:28.120
I promise.

00:17:31.306 --> 00:17:32.641
Thanks.

00:17:35.435 --> 00:17:36.880
Thank you...

00:18:18.457 --> 00:18:20.022
Find any good antiques?

00:18:20.626 --> 00:18:23.753
No, no. Got distracted.

00:18:24.398 --> 00:18:25.462
Have a drink.

00:18:25.657 --> 00:18:27.273
Yeah, thanks.

00:18:31.447 --> 00:18:34.902
So, poor guy, huh, killing himself?

00:18:36.098 --> 00:18:39.063
That kind of thing seems
to be going around lately.

00:18:39.137 --> 00:18:41.620
Yeah. Yeah, I heard
about the other ones.

00:18:41.707 --> 00:18:45.242
It's almost like this hotel
is cursed or something.

00:18:45.245 --> 00:18:47.920
Every hotel has its spilled blood.

00:18:49.488 --> 00:18:51.111
If people only knew what's going on

00:18:51.116 --> 00:18:53.290
In some of those rooms
they've checked into.

00:18:55.376 --> 00:18:57.250
You know a lot about
the place, don't you?

00:18:57.278 --> 00:18:59.063
Down to the last nail.

00:18:59.837 --> 00:19:01.683
I'd love to hear some stories.

00:19:02.575 --> 00:19:03.833
Boy,

00:19:04.238 --> 00:19:06.780
You should never say that to an old man.

00:19:10.966 --> 00:19:14.141
This is little miss Susan
and her mother, Rose.

00:19:14.508 --> 00:19:16.020
Happier days.

00:19:19.467 --> 00:19:21.110
They're not happy now?

00:19:21.488 --> 00:19:25.092
Well, would you be, leaving
the only home you ever knew?

00:19:25.956 --> 00:19:27.682
I don't know. I never really knew one.

00:19:27.706 --> 00:19:29.701
Well, this is Rose's home.

00:19:29.707 --> 00:19:31.802
Been in the family over a century.

00:19:31.876 --> 00:19:33.970
Used to be the family estate,

00:19:33.978 --> 00:19:37.563
And now she gets to live in
some senior-Living graveyard,

00:19:37.598 --> 00:19:39.662
And they tear this place down.

00:19:40.757 --> 00:19:42.350
That's too bad.

00:19:43.926 --> 00:19:46.263
I hear Rose isn't feeling well either.

00:19:46.268 --> 00:19:47.440
No, she isn't.

00:19:47.987 --> 00:19:49.083
What's wrong with her?

00:19:49.446 --> 00:19:51.432
It's not my business to say.

00:19:56.566 --> 00:19:58.200
Who's this?

00:19:58.967 --> 00:20:00.711
That's Rose

00:20:01.745 --> 00:20:03.313
When she was a little girl.

00:20:10.946 --> 00:20:12.520
Who's that with her?

00:20:12.628 --> 00:20:14.341
That's her nanny, Marie.

00:20:14.345 --> 00:20:16.992
She looked after Rose
more than her own mother.

00:20:39.786 --> 00:20:41.412
How you feeling, Sammy?

00:20:42.986 --> 00:20:46.770
I guess mixing whiskey and jager
wasn't such a gangbuster idea, was it?

00:20:49.346 --> 00:20:52.010
I'll bet you don't remember a
thing from last night, do you?

00:20:52.015 --> 00:20:54.293
No, I can still taste the tequila.

00:20:55.996 --> 00:20:58.451
You know, there's a really
good hangover remedy. It's uh...

00:20:58.537 --> 00:21:02.142
It's a greasy pork sandwich
served up in a dirty ashtray.

00:21:02.187 --> 00:21:04.040
Oh, I hate you. I know you do.

00:21:05.447 --> 00:21:07.823
Hey, turns out when
grandma Rose was a tyke,

00:21:08.475 --> 00:21:11.773
She had a creole nanny
who wore a hoodoo necklace.

00:21:13.417 --> 00:21:15.971
So you think she taught
Rose hoodoo? Yes, I do.

00:21:18.236 --> 00:21:19.270
All right.

00:21:21.446 --> 00:21:23.610
I think it's time we talk to Rose, then.

00:21:23.715 --> 00:21:25.661
Oh, you need to brush your teeth first.

00:21:35.887 --> 00:21:36.983
Hello?

00:21:38.377 --> 00:21:39.752
Susan?

00:21:41.496 --> 00:21:42.533
Clear?

00:23:07.498 --> 00:23:09.053
Mrs. Thompson?

00:23:12.685 --> 00:23:14.373
Mrs. Thompson?

00:23:17.407 --> 00:23:18.631
Rose?

00:23:21.818 --> 00:23:25.152
Hi, Mrs. Thompson. We're not
here to hurt you. It's okay. We...

00:23:29.088 --> 00:23:30.412
Rose?

00:23:35.936 --> 00:23:36.692
Dean.

00:23:40.447 --> 00:23:42.220
This woman's had a stroke.

00:23:43.497 --> 00:23:45.493
Yeah, but hoodoo's hands-On. Yeah.

00:23:45.497 --> 00:23:48.111
You got to mix herbs and
chant, build an altar.

00:23:48.415 --> 00:23:50.023
So it can't be Rose.

00:23:50.058 --> 00:23:52.921
Hey, maybe it's not even hoodoo.
You know, she could be faking.

00:23:52.956 --> 00:23:54.762
What do you want to do,
poke her with a stick?

00:23:55.967 --> 00:23:57.911
Dude, you're not gonna
poke her with a stick.

00:23:57.995 --> 00:23:59.351
What the hell?

00:23:59.398 --> 00:24:00.921
What are you doing in here?

00:24:01.247 --> 00:24:02.861
We just wanted to talk to Rose.

00:24:02.898 --> 00:24:04.732
Look at her. She's
scared out of her wits.

00:24:04.828 --> 00:24:06.910
I want you out of my
hotel in two minutes

00:24:06.918 --> 00:24:08.160
Or I'm calling the cops.

00:24:25.276 --> 00:24:27.300
Your turn. Eightsies.

00:24:33.988 --> 00:24:35.622
Have you started packing yet?

00:24:35.636 --> 00:24:37.242
No. Why not?

00:24:37.317 --> 00:24:38.671
I don't want to move.

00:24:38.735 --> 00:24:41.192
Yes, I know, but we have to.

00:24:41.216 --> 00:24:43.291
But Maggie says we're
not allowed to move.

00:24:43.335 --> 00:24:44.182
Yeah?

00:24:44.818 --> 00:24:48.621
Tyler, enough. Maggie is imaginary.

00:24:48.668 --> 00:24:51.780
You're too old to have an imaginary
friend, and I am done pretending.

00:24:55.887 --> 00:24:57.533
I don't like her.

00:25:18.877 --> 00:25:20.743
I  could lug those boxes for you.

00:25:20.746 --> 00:25:22.631
I got it, Sherwin. Thanks.

00:25:22.655 --> 00:25:24.021
Okay, then.

00:25:24.498 --> 00:25:25.792
See you later.

00:27:30.988 --> 00:27:33.260
You okay? I think so.

00:27:34.206 --> 00:27:36.093
Come on. Come on. Let's
get inside. Let's go.

00:27:39.798 --> 00:27:42.151
Whiskey. Sure.

00:27:42.186 --> 00:27:43.671
I know the feeling.

00:27:45.358 --> 00:27:47.223
What the hell happened out there?

00:27:47.988 --> 00:27:49.693
You want the truth? Of course.

00:27:49.755 --> 00:27:51.960
At first, we thought it was
some sort of a hoodoo curse,

00:27:52.425 --> 00:27:53.650
But that out there...

00:27:54.087 --> 00:27:55.900
That was definitely a spirit.

00:27:56.457 --> 00:27:57.623
Here.

00:27:58.416 --> 00:27:59.942
You're insane.

00:28:00.756 --> 00:28:01.952
It's been said.

00:28:01.976 --> 00:28:03.141
Look, I'm sorry, Susan.

00:28:03.148 --> 00:28:05.283
We don't exactly have
time to ease you into this,

00:28:05.317 --> 00:28:07.541
But we need to know when
your mother had the stroke.

00:28:07.925 --> 00:28:10.601
What does that have to do...
Just answer the question.

00:28:11.387 --> 00:28:12.703
About a month ago.

00:28:12.916 --> 00:28:14.651
Right before the killings began.

00:28:14.656 --> 00:28:15.931
You see?

00:28:16.008 --> 00:28:19.483
So what if Rose was working hoodoo,
but not to hurt anyone, to protect them?

00:28:19.588 --> 00:28:21.843
She was using the urn patterns
to ward off the spirit.

00:28:21.906 --> 00:28:23.702
Right. Until she had a
stroke and couldn't anymore.

00:28:23.716 --> 00:28:25.121
I don't believe this. Listen,

00:28:25.156 --> 00:28:27.751
That car didn't try to run
you down by itself, okay?

00:28:28.607 --> 00:28:32.012
I mean, I guess it did technically,
but with a spirit. Forget it.

00:28:32.015 --> 00:28:33.162
Just believe what you want, alright?

00:28:33.215 --> 00:28:35.292
But the fact is you and
your family are in danger.

00:28:35.388 --> 00:28:37.371
So you need to clear
everybody out of here.

00:28:37.447 --> 00:28:38.780
Your employees,

00:28:38.786 --> 00:28:39.860
Your mother,

00:28:39.867 --> 00:28:41.592
Your daughters, everyone.

00:28:43.966 --> 00:28:47.191
I only have one daughter. One?

00:28:47.235 --> 00:28:48.923
I thought Tyler had
a sister named Maggie.

00:28:49.956 --> 00:28:51.670
Maggie's imaginary.

00:28:54.288 --> 00:28:55.361
Where's Tyler?

00:29:01.347 --> 00:29:03.712
She's going to stay here with me,

00:29:04.408 --> 00:29:06.382
And you can't stop me.

00:29:06.847 --> 00:29:10.063
There's nothing you can do about it.

00:29:12.448 --> 00:29:15.281
Maggie, don't. You're not
supposed to bother grandma.

00:29:15.998 --> 00:29:16.841
I know.

00:29:18.967 --> 00:29:20.202
Come on.

00:29:21.278 --> 00:29:22.750
Let's play.

00:29:23.268 --> 00:29:25.223
Can we have a tea party?

00:29:40.188 --> 00:29:41.333
Tyler!

00:29:45.616 --> 00:29:48.260
Oh, my god! Tyler!

00:29:52.707 --> 00:29:54.153
She's not here!

00:29:56.495 --> 00:29:57.503
Susan,

00:29:57.928 --> 00:30:00.000
Tell us what you know
about Maggie. Not much.

00:30:00.078 --> 00:30:02.102
Tyler's been talking about
her since mom got sick.

00:30:02.146 --> 00:30:03.753
Okay, did you ever know
anyone by that name?

00:30:03.755 --> 00:30:05.072
Uh no. Think, think.

00:30:05.097 --> 00:30:07.281
Somebody that could have lived
here, might have passed away.

00:30:07.715 --> 00:30:10.383
My god... My mom had
a sister named Margaret.

00:30:10.418 --> 00:30:11.450
She barely spoke about her.

00:30:11.458 --> 00:30:13.340
Did Margaret die here
when she was a kid?

00:30:13.428 --> 00:30:15.213
Yeah, she drowned in the pool.

00:30:16.125 --> 00:30:17.052
Come on.

00:30:36.415 --> 00:30:38.143
I don't like it up here.

00:30:38.146 --> 00:30:39.881
I'm scared.

00:30:39.986 --> 00:30:41.580
It's okay.

00:30:41.586 --> 00:30:43.522
All you have to do is jump.

00:30:46.435 --> 00:30:48.193
I can't swim.

00:30:48.277 --> 00:30:49.381
I know.

00:30:49.906 --> 00:30:51.351
But it won't hurt.

00:30:51.377 --> 00:30:52.550
I promise.

00:30:52.625 --> 00:30:55.802
And then we can be together forever,

00:30:55.807 --> 00:30:58.161
And no one will bother us.

00:31:02.616 --> 00:31:05.103
Why don't you just
come with me and mommy?

00:31:05.178 --> 00:31:08.861
Because I can't leave here,
and you can't leave me.

00:31:12.498 --> 00:31:13.913
Please.

00:31:13.937 --> 00:31:15.620
I don't want to be alone.

00:31:29.475 --> 00:31:30.702
Tyler!

00:31:35.757 --> 00:31:36.961
Mommy!

00:31:43.218 --> 00:31:44.461
Is there another entrance?

00:31:44.515 --> 00:31:46.160
Around back. All right, let's go!

00:31:46.216 --> 00:31:47.133
Keep working.

00:32:11.985 --> 00:32:14.070
It'll all be over soon.

00:32:15.978 --> 00:32:16.932
Stand back.

00:32:19.945 --> 00:32:21.553
Son of a bitch.

00:32:28.427 --> 00:32:29.950
Margaret...

00:32:32.475 --> 00:32:34.532
Margaret...

00:33:38.258 --> 00:33:39.751
Oh, thank god. Thank god!

00:33:40.198 --> 00:33:41.300
Mommy?

00:33:41.365 --> 00:33:42.833
Yeah, baby, I'm here.

00:33:43.466 --> 00:33:46.012
Tyler, do you see Maggie anywhere?

00:33:47.515 --> 00:33:49.030
No, she's gone.

00:34:01.955 --> 00:34:03.802
You'd really do that for me?

00:34:10.466 --> 00:34:11.892
Yes...

00:34:11.966 --> 00:34:13.411
If you did,

00:34:13.916 --> 00:34:15.450
I'd let them go.

00:34:17.678 --> 00:34:19.552
But I don't understand.

00:34:19.595 --> 00:34:22.463
You kept me away for so long.

00:34:23.246 --> 00:34:25.810
I thought you didn't love me anymore.

00:34:30.376 --> 00:34:31.610
Okay...

00:34:32.235 --> 00:34:33.690
Little sister.

00:34:48.616 --> 00:34:50.380
Don't worry, honey. We're
leaving in two minutes.

00:34:50.477 --> 00:34:51.610
We just got to get grandma.

00:34:54.885 --> 00:34:56.563
I don't get it. Did Maggie just stop?

00:34:58.115 --> 00:35:00.402
Seems like it. Where
the hell did she go?

00:35:29.437 --> 00:35:31.441
Paramedics said it was another stroke.

00:35:32.476 --> 00:35:33.501
Do you think...

00:35:34.025 --> 00:35:36.303
Margaret could have had
something to do with it?

00:35:36.967 --> 00:35:38.042
We don't know.

00:35:38.138 --> 00:35:39.460
But it's possible,

00:35:39.468 --> 00:35:40.660
Yeah.

00:35:43.375 --> 00:35:45.001
Susan, I'm sorry.

00:35:45.538 --> 00:35:47.752
You have nothing to apologize for.

00:35:47.788 --> 00:35:50.070
You've given me everything.

00:35:52.935 --> 00:35:54.103
Ready to go, kiddo?

00:35:54.125 --> 00:35:55.372
Yeah.

00:35:55.997 --> 00:35:58.230
Tyler, you're sure
Maggie's not around anymore?

00:35:58.288 --> 00:36:00.190
I'm sure. I'd see her.

00:36:05.645 --> 00:36:07.982
I guess whatever's
going on must be over.

00:36:13.158 --> 00:36:15.282
You two take care of
yourselves, all right?

00:36:19.735 --> 00:36:21.061
Thank you.

00:36:21.597 --> 00:36:22.603
Yeah.

00:36:22.608 --> 00:36:23.982
Both of you.

00:36:33.445 --> 00:36:36.021
Think you could have hooked
up some milf action there, bud.

00:36:36.026 --> 00:36:37.981
Serious, I think she liked you. Yeah,

00:36:37.997 --> 00:36:39.531
That's all she needs.

00:36:39.617 --> 00:36:41.783
Well, you saved the
mommy, you saved the girl.

00:36:41.785 --> 00:36:43.080
Not a bad day.

00:36:43.186 --> 00:36:44.933
'Course,you know, I could
have saved them myself,

00:36:45.015 --> 00:36:46.681
But I didn't want you to feel useless.

00:36:47.108 --> 00:36:48.701
All right, I appreciate it.

00:36:49.425 --> 00:36:51.661
Feels good getting back
in the saddle, doesn't it?

00:36:52.947 --> 00:36:53.910
Yeah.

00:36:54.747 --> 00:36:56.120
Yeah, it does.

00:36:56.147 --> 00:36:58.840
But it doesn't change what we
talked about last night, Dean.

00:37:00.426 --> 00:37:02.403
We talked about a lot
of things last night.

00:37:03.255 --> 00:37:05.071
You know what I mean. You were wasted.

00:37:05.177 --> 00:37:06.060
But you weren't...

00:37:07.188 --> 00:37:08.700
And you promised.



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
